# ZZZ mods

Before you answer or edit anything about a Zenless Zone Zero mod, ZZMI, a character skin, oil, or Glossify, read `docs/zzz-mod-architecture.md` and follow it.

Live mods: `C:\Users\Ika\Desktop\zzz\FlairX Mod Manager\app\XXMI\ZZMI\Mods`

Phoenix Reffaella is the working character-mod shape. This repo is Glossify. Glossify does not replace meshes.

- Put character maps in `Resource\ZZMI\...` and call `CommandList\ZZMI\SetTextures`. Do not assign `ps-t` for those maps. `ps-t0` is the shadow map.
- On a raw hash, one TextureOverride wins. `checktextureoverride` runs every match. A section that sets `match_priority` runs before one that leaves it unset, so Glossify `-1` runs before a mod at the default.
- Do not store a hash in a `persist` variable.
- Do not edit `Matcap_ZZZ.ini`. Keep one `namespace = KatFXMatcap`. OilSkin 2 is the loaded engine. Style is Numpad *, 0 through 7. 0 is off. Rebinds are the Glossify `[Key]` sections. Players change them in FlairX by pressing a key. The panel reads that line. `$oilKeysEnabled` stays 0 so the oil numpad keys do not stack.
- Restore `$oilSkin` and `$oilStrength` before the next mesh calls OilSkin. Present already clears t124–t127.
- Do not draw a stock index list into a mod vertex buffer. Do not replace the face sheen with a body oil pass.
- `DISABLED_` is off. F10 reloads. Ctrl+Alt+F10 wipes persisted values.

```
hash = 9040e2c4
match_first_index = 0
ib = ResourcePhoenixBodyAIB
Resource\ZZMI\Diffuse = ref ResourcePhoenixBodyADiffuse
run = CommandList\ZZMI\SetTextures
drawindexed = 8484, 0, 0
```
